//! GCC (Google Congestion Control) sender-side bandwidth estimator.
//!
//! Reads TWCC feedback packets generated by the remote [`TwccReceiverInterceptor`] and
//! estimates available send bandwidth with the engine's GCC estimator ([`Gcc`], the one
//! [`configure_congestion_control`] and the default interceptors run), following
//! draft-ietf-rmcat-gcc-02
//! (Holmer et al., "A Google Congestion Control Algorithm for Real-Time Communication").
//! (RFC 8698 is NADA, a different algorithm, and is not what this implements.)
//!
//! What this module adds is the shape: a pull-style [`GccHandle`] an application polls, in a
//! chain without a pacer. The estimator is the same in both shapes. Until v0.22.0+brainwires.6
//! this interceptor had an estimator of its own (a trendline filter and one AIMD estimate),
//! which departed from the draft in three ways that this scenario shows: a link capped at
//! 300 kbit/s had its estimate cut to the floor by a second of loss and climb back at 8% a
//! second, over and over.
//!
//! - Section 6: the loss-based estimate As_hat is its own ("As long as less than 2% of the
//!   packets have been lost As_hat(i) will be increased as As_hat(i) = 1.05(As_hat(i-1))",
//!   "The actual sending rate is set as the minimum between As_hat and A_hat"). The old
//!   estimator applied the loss cut to the delay-based estimate, which only climbs 8% a second.
//! - Section 5.5: on over-use "A_hat(i) = beta * R_hat(i)", the received rate. The old one
//!   multiplied its estimate by 0.85.
//! - Section 5.5: "A_hat(i) < 1.5 * R_hat(i)". The old one had no such bound: its estimate
//!   climbed to the maximum whatever was sent. Now the estimate is not increased past the
//!   bound, and one that is above it is held.
//!
//! What an application polling the handle notices: the estimate no longer runs ahead of what
//! is sent (it is not increased past one and a half times the rate the receiver reports as
//! arriving); an estimate once reached is kept while the application sends less (audio
//! alone, a camera turned off), and is lowered by over-use, by loss and by feedback that
//! stops while packets are sent, which halves it ([`Gcc::with_feedback_timeout`]), and by
//! nothing else ([`ReceivedRateBound`]); a REMB or a TMMBR from the peer bounds it.
//!
//! [`Gcc`]: crate::Gcc
//! [`Gcc::with_feedback_timeout`]: crate::Gcc::with_feedback_timeout
//! [`ReceivedRateBound`]: crate::ReceivedRateBound
//! [`configure_congestion_control`]: https://docs.rs/rtc
//!
//! # Chain position
//!
//! GCC must sit **nearer the wire** than [`TwccSenderInterceptor`] so that `handle_write`
//! sees packets after the TWCC sequence number has already been stamped. Put it in
//! [`Slot::CongestionControl`](crate::Slot::CongestionControl), below
//! [`Slot::TwccSender`](crate::Slot::TwccSender):
//!
//! ```text
//! Registry::new()
//!     .with(Slot::CongestionControl, PassThroughInterceptor::new().with(gcc_builder.build()))
//!     .with(Slot::TwccSender, TwccSenderBuilder::new().build())
//! ```
//!
//! Writes walk away from the application toward the wire: TwccSender stamps first, then
//! GCC reads it. TWCC feedback reads reach GCC first, on their way to the application.
//!
//! GCC is a nested interceptor, so it needs an inner end: use
//! [`PassThroughInterceptor`](crate::PassThroughInterceptor), never
//! [`NoopInterceptor`](crate::NoopInterceptor). The latter is the chain's RTCP terminus; wrapped
//! in this slot, the first one inbound packets reach, it would end every RTCP packet nothing
//! marked (NACKs, receiver reports, PLI and FIR) before any other interceptor or the application
//! saw it.
//!
//! # Usage
//!
//! ```ignore
//! use rtci_interceptor::{
//!     GccInterceptorBuilder, Interceptor, PassThroughInterceptor, Registry, Slot,
//!     TwccSenderBuilder,
//! };
//!
//! let (gcc_builder, gcc_handle) = GccInterceptorBuilder::new();
//! let chain = Registry::new()
//!     .with(Slot::CongestionControl, PassThroughInterceptor::new().with(gcc_builder.build()))
//!     .with(Slot::TwccSender, TwccSenderBuilder::new().build())
//!     .build();
//!
//! // In the application polling loop:
//! if let Some(bps) = gcc_handle.target_bitrate_bps() {
//!     encoder.set_bitrate(bps);
//! }
//! ```
//!
//! [`TwccSenderInterceptor`]: crate::TwccSenderInterceptor
//! [`TwccReceiverInterceptor`]: crate::TwccReceiverInterceptor

use crate::cc::estimator::EstimatorStats;
use crate::cc::interceptor::{
    CongestionControlBuilder, CongestionControlHandle, CongestionControlInterceptor,
};
use crate::gcc::estimator::{DEFAULT_INITIAL_BITRATE, Gcc};
use crate::gcc::rate_control::ReceivedRateBound;
use crate::stream_info::StreamInfo;
use crate::{Interceptor, Packet, TaggedPacket, interceptor};
use rtcp::transport_feedbacks::transport_layer_cc::TransportLayerCc;
use sansio::Protocol;
use shared::error::Error;
use std::marker::PhantomData;
use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};

/// Shared state written by [`GccInterceptor`] and read by [`GccHandle`].
pub struct GccShared {
    /// The target for the original media, in bits per second: the estimate less the NACK
    /// responder's retransmission reserve (RFC 4588 section 7). `None` until the first TWCC
    /// feedback has been processed.
    pub target_bitrate_bps: Option<u32>,
    /// Latest estimated available send bandwidth, in bits per second: what the original media
    /// and the retransmissions share. `None` until the first TWCC feedback has been processed.
    pub estimate_bps: Option<u32>,
    /// The retransmission reserve the NACK responder announced last
    /// ([`RetransmissionReserve`](crate::RetransmissionReserve)), in bits per second.
    pub retransmission_reserve_bps: f64,
    /// The estimator's two halves and its smoothed loss.
    pub stats: EstimatorStats,
}

impl GccShared {
    /// The target for the original media: the estimate less the reserve, never under the
    /// controller's `minimum` (what the application set to carry its media at the least).
    fn update_target(&mut self, minimum: u32) {
        self.target_bitrate_bps = self.estimate_bps.map(|estimate| {
            let lowered = (f64::from(estimate) - self.retransmission_reserve_bps).max(0.0) as u32;
            lowered.max(minimum.min(estimate))
        });
    }
}

/// Read-only handle to the latest GCC bandwidth estimate.
///
/// Clone-able and thread-safe — share freely across application threads.
#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct GccHandle {
    inner: Arc<Mutex<GccShared>>,
}

impl GccHandle {
    fn shared(&self) -> std::sync::MutexGuard<'_, GccShared> {
        self.inner.lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| {
            log::warn!("gcc: shared mutex poisoned, recovering last estimate");
            e.into_inner()
        })
    }

    /// The target an encoder follows, in bps: the estimate less the retransmission reserve
    /// the NACK responder holds while it repairs (RFC 4588 section 7: "the sender SHOULD NOT
    /// send retransmission packets without reducing the packet rate and bitrate of the
    /// original stream"), never under the minimum bit rate
    /// ([`GccInterceptorBuilder::with_min_bitrate`]). The estimate itself while nothing is
    /// being repaired, and in a chain without a NACK responder. `None` if no TWCC feedback has been processed yet.
    pub fn target_bitrate_bps(&self) -> Option<u32> {
        self.shared().target_bitrate_bps
    }

    /// The latest estimated available send bandwidth in bps, which the original media and
    /// the retransmissions share; `None` if no TWCC feedback has been processed yet.
    pub fn estimate_bps(&self) -> Option<u32> {
        self.shared().estimate_bps
    }

    /// The estimator's two halves (draft-ietf-rmcat-gcc-02 sections 5 and 6: the estimate is
    /// the lower of the delay-based and the loss-based one), its smoothed loss fraction and
    /// the round-trip time it works with.
    pub fn stats(&self) -> EstimatorStats {
        self.shared().stats
    }
}

/// Builder for [`GccInterceptor`].
///
/// Create with [`GccInterceptorBuilder::new`], which returns `(builder, handle)`.
pub struct GccInterceptorBuilder<P> {
    min_bitrate_bps: u32,
    max_bitrate_bps: u32,
    received_rate_bound: ReceivedRateBound,
    shared: Arc<Mutex<GccShared>>,
    _phantom: PhantomData<P>,
}

impl<P> GccInterceptorBuilder<P> {
    /// Create a new builder and the associated [`GccHandle`].
    ///
    /// The handle can be shared with the application so it can read the
    /// latest bitrate estimate each polling tick.
    pub fn new() -> (Self, GccHandle) {
        let shared = Arc::new(Mutex::new(GccShared {
            target_bitrate_bps: None,
            estimate_bps: None,
            retransmission_reserve_bps: 0.0,
            stats: EstimatorStats::default(),
        }));
        let handle = GccHandle {
            inner: shared.clone(),
        };
        let builder = Self {
            min_bitrate_bps: 30_000,
            max_bitrate_bps: 2_500_000,
            received_rate_bound: ReceivedRateBound::default(),
            shared,
            _phantom: PhantomData,
        };
        (builder, handle)
    }

    /// Minimum send rate floor (default 30 kbps).
    pub fn with_min_bitrate(mut self, bps: u32) -> Self {
        self.min_bitrate_bps = bps;
        self
    }

    /// Maximum send rate ceiling (default 2.5 Mbps).
    pub fn with_max_bitrate(mut self, bps: u32) -> Self {
        self.max_bitrate_bps = bps;
        self
    }

    /// What the bound of the estimate by the received rate does to an estimate above it
    /// ([`Gcc::with_received_rate_bound`](crate::Gcc::with_received_rate_bound)): by default
    /// it only stops the increase, so the estimate is kept while the application sends less
    /// than it.
    pub fn with_received_rate_bound(mut self, received_rate_bound: ReceivedRateBound) -> Self {
        self.received_rate_bound = received_rate_bound;
        self
    }

    /// Build the interceptor factory closure.
    pub fn build(self) -> impl FnOnce(P) -> GccInterceptor<P> {
        move |inner| {
            let (min, max) = (
                f64::from(self.min_bitrate_bps),
                f64::from(self.max_bitrate_bps).max(f64::from(self.min_bitrate_bps)),
            );
            // The estimate starts at 300 kbit/s, and starts over from there on a new path.
            let estimator = Gcc::new(DEFAULT_INITIAL_BITRATE, min, max)
                .with_received_rate_bound(self.received_rate_bound);
            let (control, handle) = CongestionControlBuilder::new(estimator).build_with_handle();
            GccInterceptor {
                inner,
                control,
                handle,
                min_bitrate_bps: self.min_bitrate_bps,
                fed_back: false,
                shared: self.shared,
            }
        }
    }
}

/// Sender-side GCC bandwidth estimator interceptor.
///
/// Every outgoing RTP packet (stamped with its transport-wide sequence number) and every
/// incoming RTCP packet goes through the engine's congestion control interceptor
/// ([`CongestionControlInterceptor`] around [`Gcc`]); the resulting estimate is written to
/// the [`GccHandle`] shared state.
#[derive(Interceptor)]
pub struct GccInterceptor<P> {
    #[next]
    inner: P,

    /// The send history, the feedback ingest and the estimator.
    control: CongestionControlInterceptor<Gcc>,
    handle: CongestionControlHandle,
    /// The estimator's floor.
    min_bitrate_bps: u32,
    /// Whether transport-wide feedback has been read (the handle reports nothing before).
    fed_back: bool,

    /// Shared state — written here, read via [`GccHandle`].
    shared: Arc<Mutex<GccShared>>,
}

#[interceptor]
impl<P: Interceptor> GccInterceptor<P> {
    /// Outgoing packets pass the controller, which records each RTP packet's size and
    /// departure under its transport-wide sequence number.
    ///
    /// Must be inner to [`TwccSenderInterceptor`](crate::TwccSenderInterceptor) so the sequence number has
    /// already been stamped by the time this method is called.
    #[overrides]
    fn handle_write(&mut self, msg: TaggedPacket) -> Result<(), Self::Error> {
        // The NACK responder's retransmission reserve, which the target for the original
        // media leaves out.
        if let Some(reserve) = msg.message.custom::<crate::RetransmissionReserve>()
            && reserve.bits_per_second.is_finite()
        {
            let mut shared = self.shared.lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner());
            shared.retransmission_reserve_bps = reserve.bits_per_second.max(0.0);
            shared.update_target(self.min_bitrate_bps);
        }
        self.control.handle_write(msg)?;
        self.forward()
    }

    /// Incoming packets pass the controller, which reads the transport-wide feedback (and the
    /// receiver reports, REMB and TMMBR) and announces the estimate on the packet that moved
    /// it, so that the NACK responder holds the retransmissions to it (it lowers the
    /// attribute by its reserve on the way to the application).
    #[overrides]
    fn handle_read(&mut self, msg: TaggedPacket) -> Result<(), Self::Error> {
        if let Packet::Rtcp(ref packets) = msg.message.packet
            && packets
                .iter()
                .any(|packet| packet.as_any().is::<TransportLayerCc>())
        {
            self.fed_back = true;
        }
        self.control.handle_read(msg)?;
        self.forward()
    }

    /// The controller's own deadlines (feedback that stops while packets are sent).
    #[overrides]
    fn handle_timeout(&mut self, now: Self::Time) -> Result<(), Self::Error> {
        self.control.handle_timeout(now)?;
        self.forward()?;
        self.inner.handle_timeout(now)
    }

    #[overrides]
    fn poll_timeout(&mut self) -> Option<Self::Time> {
        match (self.control.poll_timeout(), self.inner.poll_timeout()) {
            (Some(a), Some(b)) => Some(a.min(b)),
            (a, b) => a.or(b),
        }
    }

    /// Register a local stream with the controller.
    #[overrides]
    fn bind_local_stream(&mut self, info: &StreamInfo) {
        self.control.bind_local_stream(info);
        self.inner.bind_local_stream(info);
    }

    /// Remove a local stream.
    #[overrides]
    fn unbind_local_stream(&mut self, info: &StreamInfo) {
        self.control.unbind_local_stream(info);
        self.inner.unbind_local_stream(info);
    }

    #[overrides]
    fn bind_remote_stream(&mut self, info: &StreamInfo) {
        self.control.bind_remote_stream(info);
        self.inner.bind_remote_stream(info);
    }

    #[overrides]
    fn unbind_remote_stream(&mut self, info: &StreamInfo) {
        self.control.unbind_remote_stream(info);
        self.inner.unbind_remote_stream(info);
    }
}

impl<P: Interceptor> GccInterceptor<P> {
    /// Hands on what the controller let through or made (either way), and publishes its
    /// estimate to the handle.
    fn forward(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error> {
        if self.fed_back {
            let mut shared = self.shared.lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| {
                log::warn!("gcc: shared mutex poisoned, recovering to publish estimate");
                e.into_inner()
            });
            shared.estimate_bps = Some(self.handle.target_bitrate() as u32);
            shared.stats = self.handle.stats();
            shared.update_target(self.min_bitrate_bps);
        }
        while let Some(msg) = self.control.poll_write() {
            self.inner.handle_write(msg)?;
        }
        while let Some(msg) = self.control.poll_read() {
            self.inner.handle_read(msg)?;
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use crate::AttributedPacket;
    use crate::{
        NoopInterceptor, PassThroughInterceptor, RTPHeaderExtension, Registry, Slot,
        twcc::TRANSPORT_CC_URI,
    };
    use rtcp::transport_feedbacks::transport_layer_cc::{
        PacketStatusChunk, RecvDelta, RunLengthChunk, StatusChunkTypeTcc, SymbolTypeTcc,
    };
    use sansio::Protocol;
    use shared::{TransportContext, TransportMessage};
    use std::time::Duration;
    use std::time::Instant;

    fn stream_info_with_twcc(ssrc: u32) -> StreamInfo {
        StreamInfo {
            ssrc,
            rtp_header_extensions: vec![RTPHeaderExtension {
                uri: TRANSPORT_CC_URI.to_string(),
                id: 5,
            }],
            ..Default::default()
        }
    }

    fn make_rtp(ssrc: u32, rtp_seq: u16, now: Instant) -> TaggedPacket {
        TransportMessage {
            now,
            transport: TransportContext::default(),
            message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtp(rtp::Packet {
                header: rtp::header::Header {
                    ssrc,
                    sequence_number: rtp_seq,
                    ..Default::default()
                },
                // A packet of a 300 kbit/s stream at fifty packets a second: the estimate
                // stays within one and a half times what the receiver reports as arriving.
                payload: bytes::Bytes::from(vec![0u8; 750]),
            })),
        }
    }

    fn make_twcc_feedback(
        base_seq: u16,
        recv_times_us: &[i64], // per-packet receive times in microseconds (absolute)
        now: Instant,
    ) -> TaggedPacket {
        let base_recv_us = recv_times_us.first().copied().unwrap_or(0);
        // reference_time is 24-bit in 64ms units.
        let reference_time = (base_recv_us / 64_000) as u32;
        let base_ref_us = reference_time as i64 * 64_000;

        let mut deltas = Vec::new();
        let mut prev_us = base_ref_us;
        for &t in recv_times_us {
            let delta_us = t - prev_us;
            deltas.push(RecvDelta {
                type_tcc_packet: SymbolTypeTcc::PacketReceivedSmallDelta,
                delta: delta_us,
            });
            prev_us = t;
        }

        let chunk = PacketStatusChunk::RunLengthChunk(RunLengthChunk {
            type_tcc: StatusChunkTypeTcc::RunLengthChunk,
            packet_status_symbol: SymbolTypeTcc::PacketReceivedSmallDelta,
            run_length: recv_times_us.len() as u16,
        });

        let fb = TransportLayerCc {
            sender_ssrc: 0,
            media_ssrc: 0,
            base_sequence_number: base_seq,
            packet_status_count: recv_times_us.len() as u16,
            reference_time,
            fb_pkt_count: 0,
            packet_chunks: vec![chunk],
            recv_deltas: deltas,
        };

        TransportMessage {
            now,
            transport: TransportContext::default(),
            message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtcp(vec![Box::new(fb)])),
        }
    }

    /// Build a chain with TwccSender (outer) → GccInterceptor (inner).
    ///
    /// GCC must be inner so `handle_write` sees TWCC-stamped packets.
    fn make_chain() -> (impl crate::Interceptor, GccHandle) {
        use crate::TwccSenderBuilder;
        let (gcc_builder, handle) = GccInterceptorBuilder::new();
        // GCC sits nearer the wire than TwccSender, so writes are stamped before GCC sees them.
        let chain = Registry::new()
            .with(
                Slot::CongestionControl,
                PassThroughInterceptor::new().with(gcc_builder.build()),
            )
            .with(Slot::TwccSender, TwccSenderBuilder::new().build())
            .build();
        (chain, handle)
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_handle_returns_estimate_after_feedback() {
        let (mut chain, handle) = make_chain();
        let ssrc = 1001u32;
        chain.bind_local_stream(&stream_info_with_twcc(ssrc));

        let base = Instant::now();
        // Send 5 packets; TwccSender will stamp seq 0..4.
        for i in 0..5u16 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(
                    ssrc,
                    i,
                    base + Duration::from_millis(i as u64 * 33),
                ))
                .unwrap();
        }

        // Feed back receive times: 33ms inter-packet spacing, 20ms constant one-way delay.
        // Units: microseconds.  20ms = 20_000µs; spacing 33ms = 33_000µs.
        let recv_us: Vec<i64> = (0..5).map(|i: i64| i * 33_000 + 20_000).collect();

        chain
            .handle_read(make_twcc_feedback(
                0,
                &recv_us,
                base + Duration::from_millis(200),
            ))
            .unwrap();

        assert!(
            handle.target_bitrate_bps().is_some(),
            "should have an estimate after feedback"
        );

        // The estimate rides out on the feedback packet, so a pacer in the chain follows it.
        let feedback = chain.poll_read().expect("the feedback carries on");
        let announced = match feedback
            .message
            .get(&crate::Attribute::TargetBitrateChanged {
                bits_per_second: 0.0,
            }) {
            Some(crate::Attribute::TargetBitrateChanged { bits_per_second }) => {
                Some(*bits_per_second as u32)
            }
            _ => None,
        };
        assert_eq!(handle.target_bitrate_bps(), announced);
    }

    /// RFC 4588 section 7: the target the handle reports for the original media is the
    /// estimate less the retransmission reserve the NACK responder sends down the write leg;
    /// the estimate itself stays readable, and the feedback announces it unlowered (the
    /// responder lowers it on its way to the application, a pacer paces at it).
    #[test]
    fn the_target_leaves_out_the_retransmission_reserve() {
        let (mut chain, handle) = make_chain();
        let ssrc = 1001u32;
        chain.bind_local_stream(&stream_info_with_twcc(ssrc));
        let base = Instant::now();
        for i in 0..5u16 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(
                    ssrc,
                    i,
                    base + Duration::from_millis(i as u64 * 33),
                ))
                .unwrap();
        }
        while chain.poll_write().is_some() {}
        let recv_us: Vec<i64> = (0..5).map(|i: i64| i * 33_000 + 20_000).collect();
        chain
            .handle_read(make_twcc_feedback(
                0,
                &recv_us,
                base + Duration::from_millis(200),
            ))
            .unwrap();
        let estimate = handle.estimate_bps().expect("an estimate");
        assert_eq!(Some(estimate), handle.target_bitrate_bps());

        let reserve = |bits_per_second: f64| TaggedPacket {
            now: base + Duration::from_millis(250),
            transport: TransportContext::default(),
            message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtcp(vec![])).with(crate::Attribute::Custom(
                Arc::new(crate::RetransmissionReserve { bits_per_second }),
            )),
        };
        chain.handle_write(reserve(100_000.0)).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(Some(estimate), handle.estimate_bps());
        assert_eq!(Some(estimate - 100_000), handle.target_bitrate_bps());

        let announced = chain.poll_read().and_then(|feedback| {
            match feedback
                .message
                .get(&crate::Attribute::TargetBitrateChanged {
                    bits_per_second: 0.0,
                }) {
                Some(crate::Attribute::TargetBitrateChanged { bits_per_second }) => {
                    Some(*bits_per_second as u32)
                }
                _ => None,
            }
        });
        assert_eq!(
            Some(estimate),
            announced,
            "the feedback carries the estimate"
        );

        chain.handle_write(reserve(0.0)).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(Some(estimate), handle.target_bitrate_bps(), "released");
    }

    /// A new path (inbound packets between new addresses, three in a row: an ICE restart, a
    /// move to another network) restarts the estimate from the start rate, and the packets
    /// sent into the old path before it no longer count: twenty lost there and five received
    /// on the new path are no loss of the new path's (counted, 80 % would cut the estimate to
    /// 60 %).
    #[test]
    fn a_new_path_starts_over_and_the_old_paths_losses_do_not_count() {
        use rtcp::transport_feedbacks::transport_layer_cc::RecvDelta;
        let (mut chain, handle) = make_chain();
        let ssrc = 1001u32;
        chain.bind_local_stream(&stream_info_with_twcc(ssrc));
        let base = Instant::now();
        let at = |ms: u64| base + Duration::from_millis(ms);
        for i in 0..10u16 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(ssrc, i, at(i as u64 * 20)))
                .unwrap();
        }
        let recv_us: Vec<i64> = (0..10).map(|i: i64| i * 20_000 + 20_000).collect();
        chain
            .handle_read(make_twcc_feedback(0, &recv_us, at(250)))
            .unwrap();
        // Into the old path, which is gone.
        for i in 10..30u16 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(ssrc, i, at(300 + i as u64 * 20)))
                .unwrap();
        }
        let new_path = TransportContext {
            local_addr: "10.0.9.1:5000".parse().unwrap(),
            peer_addr: "10.0.0.2:5000".parse().unwrap(),
            ..Default::default()
        };
        for k in 0..3u64 {
            chain
                .handle_read(TaggedPacket {
                    now: at(1_000 + k),
                    transport: new_path,
                    message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtcp(vec![Box::new(
                        rtcp::receiver_report::ReceiverReport {
                            ssrc: 42,
                            ..Default::default()
                        },
                    )])),
                })
                .unwrap();
        }
        assert_eq!(Some(300_000), handle.estimate_bps(), "the start rate");
        for i in 30..35u16 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(ssrc, i, at(1_000 + i as u64 * 20)))
                .unwrap();
        }
        while chain.poll_write().is_some() {}
        while chain.poll_read().is_some() {}
        // Feedback on the new path: 10..29 lost, 30..34 received 20 ms apart.
        let reference_time = (1_600_000i64 / 64_000) as u32;
        let mut recv = reference_time as i64 * 64_000;
        let deltas = (0..5)
            .map(|k| {
                let t = 1_620_000 + k * 20_000;
                let delta = t - recv;
                recv = t;
                RecvDelta {
                    type_tcc_packet: SymbolTypeTcc::PacketReceivedSmallDelta,
                    delta,
                }
            })
            .collect();
        let run = |symbol, run_length| {
            PacketStatusChunk::RunLengthChunk(RunLengthChunk {
                type_tcc: StatusChunkTypeTcc::RunLengthChunk,
                packet_status_symbol: symbol,
                run_length,
            })
        };
        let fb = TransportLayerCc {
            base_sequence_number: 10,
            packet_status_count: 25,
            reference_time,
            packet_chunks: vec![
                run(SymbolTypeTcc::PacketNotReceived, 20),
                run(SymbolTypeTcc::PacketReceivedSmallDelta, 5),
            ],
            recv_deltas: deltas,
            ..Default::default()
        };
        chain
            .handle_read(TaggedPacket {
                now: at(1_800),
                transport: new_path,
                message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtcp(vec![Box::new(fb)])),
            })
            .unwrap();
        let estimate = handle.estimate_bps().unwrap();
        assert!(
            estimate >= 300_000,
            "cut to {estimate} for the old path's losses"
        );
    }

    /// The peer connection's word that it selected another candidate pair
    /// ([`crate::PathChanged`]) is a new path also when every packet keeps its addresses (a
    /// TURN relay that keeps them, an application that hands datagrams over with one
    /// placeholder pair): the estimate starts over from the start rate, announced on the
    /// carrier for a pacer, and twenty packets sent into the old path before it are no loss of
    /// the new path's (counted, 80 % would cut the estimate to 60 %).
    #[test]
    fn the_peer_connections_path_change_starts_over_with_the_same_addresses() {
        let (mut chain, handle) = make_chain();
        let ssrc = 1001u32;
        chain.bind_local_stream(&stream_info_with_twcc(ssrc));
        let base = Instant::now();
        let at = |ms: u64| base + Duration::from_millis(ms);
        for i in 0..10u16 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(ssrc, i, at(i as u64 * 20)))
                .unwrap();
        }
        // Climb a while above the start rate, on feedback of a clean path.
        let mut next = 10u16;
        for round in 0..30u64 {
            let first = next - 10;
            let recv_us: Vec<i64> = (0..10)
                .map(|k: i64| (round as i64 * 200_000) + k * 20_000 + 20_000)
                .collect();
            chain
                .handle_read(make_twcc_feedback(first, &recv_us, at(round * 200 + 250)))
                .unwrap();
            for i in next..next + 10 {
                chain
                    .handle_write(make_rtp(
                        ssrc,
                        i,
                        at((round + 1) * 200 + (i - next) as u64 * 20),
                    ))
                    .unwrap();
            }
            next += 10;
        }
        while chain.poll_write().is_some() {}
        while chain.poll_read().is_some() {}
        let climbed = handle.estimate_bps().unwrap();
        assert!(climbed > 300_000, "climbed to {climbed}");
        // Packets `next - 10 .. next + 20` go into the old path, which is gone.
        for i in next..next + 20 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(ssrc, i, at(6_400 + (i - next) as u64 * 20)))
                .unwrap();
        }
        let lost_from = next - 10;
        next += 20;
        chain
            .handle_read(crate::PathChanged.into_packet(at(7_000), None))
            .unwrap();
        assert_eq!(Some(300_000), handle.estimate_bps(), "the start rate");
        let carrier = chain.poll_read().expect("the carrier goes on");
        assert!(carrier.message.custom::<crate::PathChanged>().is_some());
        let announced = match carrier
            .message
            .get(&crate::Attribute::TargetBitrateChanged {
                bits_per_second: 0.0,
            }) {
            Some(crate::Attribute::TargetBitrateChanged { bits_per_second }) => {
                Some(*bits_per_second as u32)
            }
            _ => None,
        };
        assert_eq!(Some(300_000), announced, "announced for a pacer");
        for i in next..next + 5 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(ssrc, i, at(7_000 + (i - next) as u64 * 20)))
                .unwrap();
        }
        while chain.poll_write().is_some() {}
        // Feedback on the new path, on the same addresses as ever: the thirty packets of the
        // old path lost, the five of the new one received 20 ms apart.
        let reference_time = (7_600_000i64 / 64_000) as u32;
        let mut recv = reference_time as i64 * 64_000;
        let deltas = (0..5)
            .map(|k| {
                let t = 7_620_000 + k * 20_000;
                let delta = t - recv;
                recv = t;
                RecvDelta {
                    type_tcc_packet: SymbolTypeTcc::PacketReceivedSmallDelta,
                    delta,
                }
            })
            .collect();
        let run = |symbol, run_length| {
            PacketStatusChunk::RunLengthChunk(RunLengthChunk {
                type_tcc: StatusChunkTypeTcc::RunLengthChunk,
                packet_status_symbol: symbol,
                run_length,
            })
        };
        let fb = TransportLayerCc {
            base_sequence_number: lost_from,
            packet_status_count: 35,
            reference_time,
            packet_chunks: vec![
                run(SymbolTypeTcc::PacketNotReceived, 30),
                run(SymbolTypeTcc::PacketReceivedSmallDelta, 5),
            ],
            recv_deltas: deltas,
            ..Default::default()
        };
        chain
            .handle_read(TaggedPacket {
                now: at(7_800),
                transport: TransportContext::default(),
                message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtcp(vec![Box::new(fb)])),
            })
            .unwrap();
        let estimate = handle.estimate_bps().unwrap();
        assert!(
            estimate >= 300_000,
            "cut to {estimate} for the old path's losses"
        );
    }

    /// The target rides with the controller's minimum (`MinimumTarget`), so the NACK
    /// responder knows where the original media cannot be lowered further.
    #[test]
    fn the_target_carries_the_controllers_minimum() {
        let (gcc_builder, _handle) = GccInterceptorBuilder::new();
        let mut chain = Registry::new()
            .with(
                Slot::CongestionControl,
                PassThroughInterceptor::new().with(gcc_builder.with_min_bitrate(123_000).build()),
            )
            .with(Slot::TwccSender, crate::TwccSenderBuilder::new().build())
            .build();
        let ssrc = 1001u32;
        chain.bind_local_stream(&stream_info_with_twcc(ssrc));
        let base = Instant::now();
        for i in 0..5u16 {
            chain
                .handle_write(make_rtp(
                    ssrc,
                    i,
                    base + Duration::from_millis(i as u64 * 33),
                ))
                .unwrap();
        }
        while chain.poll_write().is_some() {}
        let recv_us: Vec<i64> = (0..5).map(|i: i64| i * 33_000 + 20_000).collect();
        chain
            .handle_read(make_twcc_feedback(
                0,
                &recv_us,
                base + Duration::from_millis(200),
            ))
            .unwrap();
        let feedback = chain.poll_read().expect("the feedback carries on");
        assert_eq!(
            Some(&crate::MinimumTarget {
                bits_per_second: 123_000.0
            }),
            feedback.message.custom::<crate::MinimumTarget>()
        );
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_no_estimate_before_feedback() {
        let (mut chain, handle) = make_chain();
        let ssrc = 2001u32;
        chain.bind_local_stream(&stream_info_with_twcc(ssrc));
        chain
            .handle_write(make_rtp(ssrc, 0, Instant::now()))
            .unwrap();
        // No feedback yet.
        assert!(handle.target_bitrate_bps().is_none());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_non_twcc_rtcp_passes_through() {
        let (mut chain, handle) = make_chain();
        let rtcp_pkt = TransportMessage {
            now: Instant::now(),
            transport: TransportContext::default(),
            message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtcp(vec![Box::new(
                rtcp::receiver_report::ReceiverReport {
                    ssrc: 42,
                    ..Default::default()
                },
            )])),
        };
        // Should not panic; non-TWCC RTCP is forwarded.
        chain.handle_read(rtcp_pkt).unwrap();
        assert!(handle.target_bitrate_bps().is_none());
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_unbind_removes_stream() {
        let (mut chain, _handle) = make_chain();
        let ssrc = 3001u32;
        let info = stream_info_with_twcc(ssrc);
        chain.bind_local_stream(&info);
        chain.unbind_remote_stream(&info); // unbind (remote stream - no-op here)
        chain.unbind_local_stream(&info);
        // No panic — stream was removed cleanly.
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_send_time_not_recorded_without_twcc_ext() {
        // RTP sent on an SSRC not bound with TWCC should not populate send_times.
        let (mut chain, _handle) = make_chain();
        let ssrc = 4001u32;
        // Bind WITHOUT TWCC ext.
        let info = StreamInfo {
            ssrc,
            rtp_header_extensions: vec![],
            ..Default::default()
        };
        chain.bind_local_stream(&info);
        // Just verify no panic and no estimate without TWCC feedback.
        chain
            .handle_write(make_rtp(ssrc, 1, Instant::now()))
            .unwrap();
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_builder_custom_bitrate_bounds() {
        let (builder, _handle) = GccInterceptorBuilder::<()>::new();
        let builder = builder
            .with_min_bitrate(100_000)
            .with_max_bitrate(5_000_000);
        assert_eq!(builder.min_bitrate_bps, 100_000);
        assert_eq!(builder.max_bitrate_bps, 5_000_000);
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_gcc_handle_clone_shares_state() {
        let (_builder, handle) = GccInterceptorBuilder::<()>::new();
        let handle2 = handle.clone();
        assert!(handle.target_bitrate_bps().is_none());
        assert!(handle2.target_bitrate_bps().is_none());
        // Write through the shared mutex.
        handle.inner.lock().unwrap().estimate_bps = Some(500_000);
        handle.inner.lock().unwrap().update_target(0);
        assert_eq!(handle2.target_bitrate_bps(), Some(500_000));
    }

    /// Counts the inbound RTCP packets that reach its slot and passes everything on.
    #[derive(Default)]
    struct RtcpSeen {
        seen: std::sync::Arc<std::sync::atomic::AtomicUsize>,
        reads: std::collections::VecDeque<TaggedPacket>,
        writes: std::collections::VecDeque<TaggedPacket>,
    }

    impl sansio::Protocol<TaggedPacket, TaggedPacket, ()> for RtcpSeen {
        type Rout = TaggedPacket;
        type Wout = TaggedPacket;
        type Eout = ();
        type Error = shared::error::Error;
        type Time = Instant;

        fn handle_read(&mut self, msg: TaggedPacket) -> Result<(), Self::Error> {
            if matches!(msg.message.packet, Packet::Rtcp(_)) {
                self.seen.fetch_add(1, std::sync::atomic::Ordering::SeqCst);
            }
            self.reads.push_back(msg);
            Ok(())
        }
        fn poll_read(&mut self) -> Option<TaggedPacket> {
            self.reads.pop_front()
        }
        fn handle_write(&mut self, msg: TaggedPacket) -> Result<(), Self::Error> {
            self.writes.push_back(msg);
            Ok(())
        }
        fn poll_write(&mut self) -> Option<TaggedPacket> {
            self.writes.pop_front()
        }
    }

    impl crate::Interceptor for RtcpSeen {
        fn bind_local_stream(&mut self, _info: &StreamInfo) {}
        fn unbind_local_stream(&mut self, _info: &StreamInfo) {}
        fn bind_remote_stream(&mut self, _info: &StreamInfo) {}
        fn unbind_remote_stream(&mut self, _info: &StreamInfo) {}
    }

    fn pli() -> TaggedPacket {
        use rtcp::payload_feedbacks::picture_loss_indication::PictureLossIndication;
        TaggedPacket {
            now: Instant::now(),
            transport: TransportContext::default(),
            message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtcp(vec![Box::new(PictureLossIndication {
                sender_ssrc: 1,
                media_ssrc: 1001,
            })])),
        }
    }

    /// GCC in its slot around `inner`, an RTCP observer application-ward of it, and the
    /// key-frame request interceptor that delivers PLI to the application. Returns how many
    /// inbound RTCP packets the observer saw and how many packets the application read.
    fn pli_through_gcc_slot<I: crate::Interceptor + 'static>(inner: I) -> (usize, usize) {
        use crate::{KeyFrameRequestInterceptor, TwccSenderBuilder};
        let (gcc_builder, _handle) = GccInterceptorBuilder::new();
        let observer = RtcpSeen::default();
        let seen = observer.seen.clone();
        let mut chain = Registry::new()
            .with(Slot::CongestionControl, inner.with(gcc_builder.build()))
            .with(Slot::TwccSender, TwccSenderBuilder::new().build())
            .with(Slot::from(3_500), observer)
            .with(Slot::KeyFrameRequests, KeyFrameRequestInterceptor::new())
            .build();
        // The first inbound packet carries the starting estimate for the chain (an attribute:
        // a terminus passes a marked packet on); the key-frame request comes after it.
        chain
            .handle_read(TaggedPacket {
                now: Instant::now(),
                transport: TransportContext::default(),
                message: AttributedPacket::new(Packet::Rtcp(vec![Box::new(
                    rtcp::receiver_report::ReceiverReport {
                        ssrc: 42,
                        ..Default::default()
                    },
                )])),
            })
            .unwrap();
        while chain.poll_read().is_some() {}
        let before = seen.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::SeqCst);
        chain.handle_read(pli()).unwrap();
        let mut delivered = 0;
        while chain.poll_read().is_some() {
            delivered += 1;
        }
        (
            seen.load(std::sync::atomic::Ordering::SeqCst) - before,
            delivered,
        )
    }

    /// With GCC registered the documented way (around a pass-through), inbound RTCP GCC doesn't
    /// consume reaches the interceptors after its slot, and a key-frame request reaches the
    /// application.
    #[test]
    fn rtcp_passes_the_gcc_slot() {
        assert_eq!(
            (1, 1),
            pli_through_gcc_slot(PassThroughInterceptor::new()),
            "the observer saw the PLI and the application read it"
        );
    }

    /// Why the inner end must not be the terminus: around `NoopInterceptor` (the recipe this
    /// module used to document), the PLI ends in GCC's slot, the first one it reaches.
    #[test]
    fn noop_inside_the_gcc_slot_ends_rtcp_there() {
        assert_eq!((0, 0), pli_through_gcc_slot(NoopInterceptor::new()));
    }
}
